fact WorkItem(id: "WI-234", description: some(value: "Operation-call-model: Model-1 redesign — reshape apply_within requirements channel from multi-entry to single-entry; Self becomes frame.requirements[0]. Supersedes WI-229. Background: the existing implementation (WI-218 through WI-233) emits multi-entry requirements channels with the dispatching slot baked into fn position (requirement_at_current(slot=N, op=op_short)). Doc revision (May 2026) committed to Model 1: single-entry channel carrying the dispatching ResolvedSortNode; runtime expansion populates the callee's frame.requirements as [Self_dict, ...impl's requires sub-instances]. Self-as-slot-0 is the resolution for the Self-bound dispatch question (e.g. Eq.neq's default body calling Eq.eq) — Self is materialized as the first slot, so the body can access it for spec-op dispatch. Scope: (a) Remove requirement_at_current(slot, op) fn-position form; for Defer sites emit apply_within(fn = <spec_op_qn>, args, requirements = [<single dispatching dict expr>]). (b) Change build_projected_requirements_list to return a single dispatching dict expression (var_ref to caller's Self slot, requirement_at_sort projection, or construct_requirement literal). (c) Refactor record_apply_within_rewrite and record_apply_within_concrete to single-entry channel. (d) Update typer's Op.requirements computation: every spec-op body's slot 0 is Self (the spec it's defined in); slots 1..N are the sort's own requires. Existing body emissions that did requirement_at_current(slot=i) for impl's i-th require now emit requirement_at_current(slot=i+1). (e) Update eval apply_within frame-push: evaluate requirements[0] as dict; frame.requirements = [dict] ++ [dict.sub_requires[i] for i in 0..N]. (f) Add spec-op dispatch branch: when fn is a spec-op symbol, look up sort_ops_table[dict.sort][op_short]. (g) Self-recursive direct calls (e.g. EqList.eq inside EqList.eq) forward Self via requirement_at_current(0). (h) Closures capture and restore Self alongside other requirement slots. Acceptance: cargo-test green; new tests pin (1) Defer call emits apply_within(fn=SpecQN.op, requirements=[<single dict>]); (2) impl frame at entry has Self at slot 0 and sub-instances at slots 1..N; (3) spec-op dispatch resolves through sort_ops_table lookup; (4) Self-bound default bodies (e.g. Eq.neq) correctly dispatch to the impl-specific Eq.eq via Self. References: docs/design/operation-call-model.md §'How bodies refer to requirements', §'Channel cardinality (v0)', §'Eval handling for requirement_at_sort and apply_within dispatch'."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-232"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-12T22:35:00Z"))
